Humanoid Vision Watch: 3D Perception Drives Next-Generation Robots
Vision sensors function as the primary perception layer for humanoid robots, supporting object recognition, depth mapping, spatial awareness, facial detection, and human-robot interaction. Stereo vision, 3D depth cameras, time-of-flight sensors, and emerging vision technologies are helping robots operate more effectively in dynamic and unstructured environments.

